  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Jewish and Palestinian activist communities for an equal and just society in Israel</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Community in Action is a volunteering and leadership development project targeting Jewish and Arab young adults from the mixed community of Jaffa and surrounding neighbourhoods in and around Tel Aviv. Participants have to be passionate about creating social change and volunteering with youth. The project provides a model set of educated young local activists, able to share a vision of peace and partnership with the city&#x2019;s youth, uprooting preconceived perceptions. The project aims to form and equip a small group of 16 young adults aged 18-25, comprising a balanced mix of Arabs and Jews, women and men, to be politically aware and have a belief in Palestinian-Jewish partnership, and be able to lead social initiatives and campaigns, promoting an equal and just society in Israel. The participants will undergo enrichment, leadership and campaign training, and will then themselves work with youth centres to tutor and mentor over 200 disadvantaged youth.</narrative>
  </description>
